WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.578
Security reports: the
complete walkthrough.

2
00:00:03.578 --> 00:00:07.772
Use every security report as
a county security officer,

3
00:00:07.772 --> 00:00:11.602
an administrator and a
platform investigator.

4
00:00:12.372 --> 00:00:16.099
We begin as Sam, a Baltimore
City security officer.

5
00:00:16.099 --> 00:00:21.469
All people and events in this video
are synthetic training examples.

6
00:00:21.836 --> 00:00:27.537
Security officers review users, sign-ins,
audit events and usage within their

7
00:00:27.537 --> 00:00:28.647
granted places.

8
00:00:28.647 --> 00:00:33.638
This role does not provide patient
records or account editing.

9
00:00:33.998 --> 00:00:37.846
Check the active profile and
working place before reviewing.

10
00:00:37.846 --> 00:00:43.042
A narrower profile narrows your reports;
regional and platform administrators can

11
00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:45.045
cover several data roots.

12
00:00:45.406 --> 00:00:49.219
Filter listed users by
name, user name or tenant.

13
00:00:49.219 --> 00:00:55.601
Review their home agency, master profile,
MFA enrollment, last sign-in and account

14
00:00:55.601 --> 00:00:56.602
status.

15
00:00:56.902 --> 00:01:00.693
Staff can appear because they
work here or hold access here.

16
00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:04.884
A home agency alone does not
describe all their permissions.

17
00:01:05.245 --> 00:01:08.526
Export users and access
for an access review.

18
00:01:08.526 --> 00:01:14.285
The export uses your permitted scope;
the filter box only filters the on-screen

19
00:01:14.285 --> 00:01:15.285
list.

20
00:01:15.405 --> 00:01:20.101
Ask an administrator to correct
unexpected access or an account problem.

21
00:01:20.101 --> 00:01:24.676
The security officer reviews
evidence without changing accounts.

22
00:01:25.037 --> 00:01:30.358
Open Sign-in activity from Administration
to investigate suspicious patterns.

23
00:01:30.358 --> 00:01:35.457
These are leads to check, not proof
that an account was compromised.

24
00:01:35.815 --> 00:01:40.259
Choose a window: one hour, one
day, seven days or thirty days.

25
00:01:40.259 --> 00:01:43.669
Show refreshes the report for that window.

26
00:01:44.034 --> 00:01:49.114
One address trying five or more accounts
or unknown names suggests password

27
00:01:49.114 --> 00:01:50.114
spraying.

28
00:01:50.114 --> 00:01:54.247
Compare the target count,
failures and first and last times.

29
00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:59.147
One account tried from at least three
addresses suggests credential stuffing.

30
00:01:59.147 --> 00:02:03.191
Follow the account link when
you need its individual history.

31
00:02:03.554 --> 00:02:08.474
Signed in after repeated failures finds
a full sign-in preceded by at least three

32
00:02:08.474 --> 00:02:10.297
failures in the previous hour.

33
00:02:10.297 --> 00:02:13.916
Compare the success address
with the failed attempts.

34
00:02:14.274 --> 00:02:18.017
Failures by address helps
identify a noisy source.

35
00:02:18.017 --> 00:02:24.032
Compare affected accounts, unknown
names, lockouts and rate-limit refusals.

36
00:02:24.397 --> 00:02:29.630
Failures by account helps distinguish one
person having trouble from failures spread

37
00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:32.210
across many accounts and addresses.

38
00:02:32.573 --> 00:02:36.668
Lockouts and refusals shows
when access was blocked and why.

39
00:02:36.668 --> 00:02:42.529
Account-free rate-limit events and unknown
names require platform investigation.

40
00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:46.316
None means no matching pattern
in this period and scope.

41
00:02:46.316 --> 00:02:51.725
It does not prove there were no attempts
elsewhere or outside the selected window.

42
00:02:52.091 --> 00:02:57.171
Export this report downloads every
report section for the selected window.

43
00:02:57.171 --> 00:03:01.896
Section names identify the pattern
represented by each CSV row.

44
00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:07.802
Open Audit log for the tamper-evident
history of views, changes and exports.

45
00:03:07.802 --> 00:03:14.340
It records actions and identifiers, rather
than copies of free-text record contents.

46
00:03:14.695 --> 00:03:20.223
Choose Sign-in and account security (all),
then Search, to see security actions

47
00:03:20.223 --> 00:03:24.122
together instead of choosing
one action at a time.

48
00:03:24.487 --> 00:03:27.650
Clear filters to return
to the whole ledger.

49
00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:33.514
Combine User, Action, Record type and
dates to answer who did what and when.

50
00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:37.745
For example, find Sam's
access-review exports.

51
00:03:37.745 --> 00:03:44.384
Choose Sam under User, Exported under
Action, and Users and access under Record

52
00:03:44.384 --> 00:03:45.384
type.

53
00:03:45.571 --> 00:03:48.857
Set From and To for the
review period, then Search.

54
00:03:48.857 --> 00:03:53.251
The count confirms whether your
combined filters found events.

55
00:03:53.615 --> 00:03:57.236
For one record, use Record
id or its all events link.

56
00:03:57.236 --> 00:04:02.212
A record link opens the record only
when your permissions allow it.

57
00:04:02.568 --> 00:04:04.186
Events are newest first.

58
00:04:04.186 --> 00:04:09.447
Choose twenty-five or one hundred per
page; use the page links to review older

59
00:04:09.447 --> 00:04:11.398
events when more exist.

60
00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:16.684
Download CSV preserves the current
filters, with at most the newest ten

61
00:04:16.684 --> 00:04:17.796
thousand events.

62
00:04:17.796 --> 00:04:21.671
Narrow the dates if you
need a smaller review set.

63
00:04:22.032 --> 00:04:27.400
County review includes scoped staff and
events on records owned there when logged.

64
00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:31.465
Older events without an owner
stamp rely on staff scope.

65
00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:36.249
Open Usage to review screen
visits and navigation.

66
00:04:36.249 --> 00:04:41.774
Choose one, seven, thirty or
ninety days, then Show usage.

67
00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:46.960
Visits by screen compares visits,
sessions and timed visits.

68
00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:53.316
Visible time is optional, capped focused
time; missing time means unknown.

69
00:04:53.675 --> 00:04:57.613
Expand Visits by active-profile
role for role totals.

70
00:04:57.613 --> 00:05:02.813
One visit can have several roles,
so adding role counts together would

71
00:05:02.813 --> 00:05:04.699
double-count visits.

72
00:05:05.066 --> 00:05:09.812
Paths into Enter a result shows
up to three preceding screens.

73
00:05:09.812 --> 00:05:15.416
Back-and-forth paths can be useful
review, not necessarily mistakes.

74
00:05:15.784 --> 00:05:20.598
The observed search-to-saved flow
is a strict four-screen sequence.

75
00:05:20.598 --> 00:05:25.987
Our seeded example illustrates navigation,
not actual patient work or staff

76
00:05:25.987 --> 00:05:27.307
performance.

77
00:05:27.607 --> 00:05:31.447
Download summary CSV saves
the report aggregates.

78
00:05:31.447 --> 00:05:37.404
Recent sessions is a limited list; the
totals above cover the whole selected

79
00:05:37.404 --> 00:05:38.410
period.

80
00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:44.488
Choose View session to inspect the ordered
screens, active profile and any retained

81
00:05:44.488 --> 00:05:46.976
sign-in or session-end events.

82
00:05:47.337 --> 00:05:50.666
Session timestamps are
UTC with milliseconds.

83
00:05:50.666 --> 00:05:56.659
Tabs can interleave; expand Visit links
and follow the predecessor when comparing

84
00:05:56.659 --> 00:05:57.926
a workflow.

85
00:05:58.226 --> 00:06:03.785
Download this page CSV exports the
current page, up to one hundred visits.

86
00:06:03.785 --> 00:06:07.265
Use session paging for additional visits.

87
00:06:07.627 --> 00:06:12.048
You can also paste a session reference
into Open a session reference.

88
00:06:12.048 --> 00:06:16.677
The reference is a reporting
identifier, not a sign-in credential.

89
00:06:17.702 --> 00:06:21.823
No retained events or no visits
can reflect scope, period,

90
00:06:21.823 --> 00:06:24.026
missing telemetry or retention.

91
00:06:24.026 --> 00:06:28.761
Browser closure alone does not
prove that someone signed out.

92
00:06:29.114 --> 00:06:32.179
We now switch to the
Maryland administrator.

93
00:06:32.179 --> 00:06:37.822
Administrators can open account pages and
act on problems that a security officer

94
00:06:37.822 --> 00:06:38.845
reports.

95
00:06:39.145 --> 00:06:43.610
Filter for Security Training
Staff 1 and open the account.

96
00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:50.169
Review the master profile to check places,
roles, access levels and grant dates.

97
00:06:50.534 --> 00:06:56.112
Sign-in history shows the latest fifty
events: time, event, reason, address,

98
00:06:56.112 --> 00:07:00.402
browser and shortened session
and attempt references.

99
00:07:00.764 --> 00:07:05.690
Correlate password and second-factor
failures, successful sessions,

100
00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:11.204
expirations, sign-outs and administrator
actions before deciding what needs

101
00:07:11.204 --> 00:07:12.401
follow-up.

102
00:07:12.701 --> 00:07:17.310
Export this account's sign-in history
downloads up to one thousand events.

103
00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:22.506
Keep the account history with the activity
and audit exports for your review.

104
00:07:22.874 --> 00:07:25.876
We now switch to the
platform administrator.

105
00:07:25.876 --> 00:07:31.470
Unknown user names belong to no county,
so they require the security investigation

106
00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:32.684
permission.

107
00:07:32.984 --> 00:07:34.590
Open Unknown user names.

108
00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:40.676
Hashes group repeated attempts at the same
name without revealing what someone typed.

109
00:07:41.038 --> 00:07:46.384
Compare attempts, addresses, first
and last times, and addresses seen.

110
00:07:46.384 --> 00:07:51.748
A hash is useful for correlation
even when a name remains hidden.

111
00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:55.625
Look up a known suspected name
without decrypting anything.

112
00:07:55.625 --> 00:08:00.731
Type the name and choose Look up to see
its attempts over the last ninety days.

113
00:08:01.094 --> 00:08:05.153
A lookup with no matches reports
no attempts in that period.

114
00:08:05.153 --> 00:08:08.124
Lookups are recorded in the audit log.

115
00:08:08.487 --> 00:08:11.564
Export the hashed list
saves hashes and counts.

116
00:08:11.564 --> 00:08:15.238
The typed names are never
included in this export.

117
00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:19.210
Use Show names only when
the investigation needs it.

118
00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:24.764
A name may contain a password entered in
the wrong box; do not copy or share the

119
00:08:24.764 --> 00:08:26.164
revealed text.

120
00:08:26.498 --> 00:08:30.148
Enter a current authenticator
code, then Show names.

121
00:08:30.148 --> 00:08:36.233
The code stays masked in this video, and
the reveal is recorded in the audit log.

122
00:08:36.588 --> 00:08:39.184
Names are revealed for this page only.

123
00:08:39.184 --> 00:08:44.377
If an encryption key is no longer
available, a name can instead appear as no

124
00:08:44.377 --> 00:08:45.870
longer readable.

125
00:08:46.228 --> 00:08:50.102
Return to Unknown user names
to restore the hashed view.

126
00:08:50.102 --> 00:08:53.200
This ends the temporary on-page reveal.

127
00:08:53.561 --> 00:08:57.609
Finally, open Audit log and
filter Action to Export.

128
00:08:57.609 --> 00:09:03.525
Report exports, unknown-name lookups
and reveals leave an audit trail of the

129
00:09:03.525 --> 00:09:05.560
investigation itself.

130
00:09:05.928 --> 00:09:10.536
Use the report that matches the
question: access for permissions,

131
00:09:10.536 --> 00:09:16.137
sign-ins for authentication, audit for
recorded actions, and usage for observed

132
00:09:16.137 --> 00:09:17.374
navigation.

133
00:09:17.674 --> 00:09:23.435
Record the scope, time window, affected
account or session, and your findings.

134
00:09:23.435 --> 00:09:28.489
Refer account and grant changes
to an authorized administrator.

135
00:09:29.667 --> 00:09:33.308
In this video you reviewed
users and access in scope,

136
00:09:33.308 --> 00:09:38.667
investigated sign-ins and account history,
filtered and exported audit events,

137
00:09:38.667 --> 00:09:43.820
traced usage paths and sessions, and
investigated unknown names at platform

138
00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:45.220
level.
